## solar-system-model

solar-system-model-ask = If the Sun is a 20 cm ball, where is the Earth and how big?
solar-system-model-title = A model of the Solar System
solar-system-model-question = Let us make a model of the Solar System with everything at one scale: the sizes and the distances. The Sun is a 20 cm ball on the school field. The planets’ sizes and distances come from NASA’s table. Where will the Earth lie, and how big will it be?
solar-system-model-choices = A 2 cm ball 2 m from the Sun-ball
solar-system-model-choices-2 = A 2 mm grain 20 m away
solar-system-model-choices-3 = A 2 mm grain 2 m away
solar-system-model-setup = A 20 cm ball (the Sun), a ruler, a tape measure, a school field and a long street; NASA’s table of the planets’ sizes, distances and periods
